# generators-common

This package owns helpers used by more than one generator pack (`deterministic-reader`, `generate-context`, `generate-entry`, `fill`, `default-token`, `routes-api`, `routes-api-converter`, `casing-strategy`, `import-generator`, `reference-verifier`, `settings`). YAML specification parsing lives in `@deterministic-code/deterministic-specifications-typescript/parser` — import `DeterministicParser`, `IDeterministic`, and specification types from there, not from this package. The parser public value surface is `DeterministicParser` only. Filename constants (`TYPES_YAML`, `ROUTES_YAML`, …) and helpers (`typeHasTag`, `primaryKeyColumn`, `uniqueLookupFields`) live in `spec-types`. `yaml-node` is internal and is not a package export. Public parser API: `DeterministicParser(reader).parse(settings)` returns `IDeterministic` (`types`, `expandedTypes`, `datasource`, `datasourceSeeds`, `services`, `routes`); also export `IDeterministicReader`. No per-document parse methods. Types live in `types.yaml` (`TYPES_YAML`) and are tagged (`datasource_type`, `view_type`, `many_to_many`, `readonly_lookup`). `expandedTypes` inlines inherit/union fields (`inherits: set` injects `id`; `dictionary` injects `name`/`value`). Persistence overlays (unique, indexes, OCC, mapping) live on `datasource`. The primary key is `primaryKeyColumn(table, type)` (`is_fixed_id` overlay, else `id`). Language packs map `field.type` as-is — they must not add `idType` / `datetimeType` on the type object or recompute those from settings. Filter with `typeHasTag`. Authored `types` are for metadata (kind, inherits, omit via `removeFields`) only. Language packs map `field.type` as-is — they must not add `idType` / `datetimeType` on the type object or recompute those from settings. The parser and routes-api IR are dialect-agnostic (YAML names, snake paths, `{param}`). HTTP param/segment casing for generated app code stays in each language pack. Identifier/file casing for generated app code goes through `createCasingStrategy` / pack `default-casing.ts`.

`IImportGenerator` is the shared path/include surface. Every method takes names (or emit files) and returns a `string`. Language packs own the concrete class and `createImportGenerator(basePath, settings)`. `other.organize_by_feature` is read only in that class constructor — never in generate-*.ts or `PackCasing`. Generators must not compose prefixes, `features/`, crate paths, or namespaces; they only call these methods. Do not add native type mapping (`type-converter` / `type-converters`) here; those stay in each language pack.

`GenerateEntry` content may carry optional `attributes: Record<string, string>`. Verifier keys only: `module`, `exports`, `namespace`, `imports`, `uses`, `namespaceRefs` (comma-separated lists). `module` / `imports` are project-relative Rel keys (`types/generated/views/user.ts`) — never `../../` specs; relative import paths are fill-time only via `IImportGenerator.spec`. Extract with `referenceAttributesFromEntries` / `pickReferenceAttributes`, then `ReferenceVerifier.verify(attrs: ReferenceAttributes[])` (strings only, not entries). `verifyContents(entries)` requires each `exports` / `uses` / namespace name to appear as an identifier in that file (catches template glue when the attribute bag used a casing helper). Call `finalizeEntries` (`verifyEntries` + `stripAttributes`) before the patch writer / zip. Cross-lane imports need an aggregate attribute list.

Language packs import this package directly. Do not copy these sources into pack `src/common/`.

`generate` is still the only export each language lane has. It takes `GenerateContext`: `{ reader, settings }` where `reader` is `{ read, exists }` (`IDeterministicReader`) and `settings` is the flat string dict.
